  "name": "Greater Bond",
  "type": "feat",
  "effects": [],
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">Through you or your benefactor’s continued pursuit of your goals, your benefactor’s reach expands into the realms of other dragons. As a result, your connection grows more powerful. When you take this feat, you can either add a new trait aligned with any benefactor you have, or add a new benefactor and a trait they have if that benefactor shares a trait that you already possess. For instance, if you have the Fire trait from a Crimson benefactor, you can choose Earth from an Ebony benefactor because you share the Fire trait.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">Your Bond of Greed also improves in one of the following ways of your choice:</span></p><ul><li><p class=\"Standard\"><strong>Empowered Bond</strong> The status bonus to a skill check with your chosen benefactor applies for its entire duration.</p></li><li><p class=\"Standard\"><strong>Emergent Bond</strong> You can cast Bond of Greed as a reaction, triggered in response to being targeted by an attack or having to make a saving throw against an effect with a trait you possess. You must choose the corresponding benefactor with that trait if you do.</p></li><li><p class=\"Standard\"><strong>Extended Bond</strong> Your Bond of Greed’s duration increases to 10 minutes.</p></li></ul><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">You can take this feat again at 14th and 20th level. Each time you do, you make a new selection for a trait or benefactor as described above and can choose an improvement to Bond of Greed you do not have.</span></p>"
    },
